== conditional replace and checksums (06 §3.11, §3.12)
replace a free key: written
replace with the entry just read: written
replace with a stale entry: changed, the other write stays: true
create over an existing key: changed
computed checksum is the body's: true; absent: none; unknown algorithm: invalid
an entry's checksum, when it carries one, is the body's: true
== round trips
get_opt a: "hello"; absent: none; get absent: absent
head a size: 5
chunk-sized body identical: true
copy: "hello"; copy of absent: absent

== ranges
[0,+3) "012"
[4,+2) "45"
[7,+3) "789"
[0,+10) "0123456789"
[7,+100) "789"
[10,+5) ""
[20,+1) ""
absent: none; length 0: invalid

== claims
five racing claims: 1 won, losers told the holder: true
later claim: held true
same body again: won
free name: won

== delete
delete: true then false
delete_multi over 2100 keys, survivors left: 0

== awkward keys
"tsync/d/x/& < > \" ' + % # ? space" round-trips: true
"tsync/d/x/\195\169lan \226\156\147" round-trips: true
listed: true
after delete_multi: 0 listed
invalid keys refused before anything: invalid invalid invalid invalid invalid

== listing
all: a,b,c,d,e
max_keys 2: a,b
empty prefix: 0

== capabilities
verified true, share_url none

== http-proxy (backends/http-proxy §12)
read-only put: refused/read_only
read-only get of an absent key: none
wrong secret: refused/denied
unserved domain get_opt: refused/denied
unserved domain head: refused/denied
a key of another route: refused/denied
capabilities: chunk 4096, concurrency 4, verified true
get_many across pages: 2500 answers
list_many: 1 folders
copy into a share manifest: refused/denied
copy out of a share manifest: refused/denied
copy within the share cache: ok
== a backend that throttles for two seconds
a read through it: ok; the peer's breaker tripped: false
== a batch read of more than the answer budget
12 objects of 3 MiB: 12 answered whole; largest answer: 24 MiB
== a data slot is held until its answer is written
another read while the 32 MiB answer waits on its peer: waits for the slot; after: answered
== unsigned bodies dripping do not hold the data slots
a signed read meanwhile: ok within 2s: true
== a 401 from a skewed clock is not remembered
while skewed: transient/link
once the clocks agree: ok
== a server without /checksum
conditional replace: refused/other, conditional PUTs sent: 0
checksum falls back to a read: none
== a captive portal answering 200 is not remembered
behind the portal: corrupt/other; once past it: ok
== watch
behind: returned at once true
a change wakes the watch before a poll would: true
a stop answers a held watch, closing in under 2s: true
